passes clean.","cargo fmt --all --check passes clean.","ShrimpHatched event is properly defined in EventKind enum (events.rs:20) and emitted during successful clutch resolution (shrimp.rs:966-976) with EventCause::RoutineAction.","test_mature_stable_tank_breeds_well now asserts both berried_events >= 3 AND hatched_events >= 3, confirming complete reproductive cycles rather than just spawning starts.","test_neglected_tank_breeding_stalls verifies chemistry degradation (TAN > 0.5 or NO2 > 0.2 AND instability > 0.15), population stalls (no more than +5 from initial), fewer berried events than maintained control, and active dominant suppression factor.","reproductive_readiness_factors() computes all 8 named factors: temperature, condition, minerals, stability, molt_stress, density, tan, nitrite — each backed by species parameters in neocaridina_davidi.toml and ShrimpRuntimeParams.","TankSnapshot exposes repro_dominant_suppression field via dominant_repro_suppression_label() covering all 8 factors. Tests verify correct label attribution for temperature, molt_stress, tan, nitrite, and minerals scenarios.","Nitrogen cycle trace in engine.rs uses tan_oxidized_mg (AOB + comammox) — not total_n_nitrified — as the nitrogen basis paired with alkalinity consumption, ensuring stoichiometric consistency even during nitrite accumulation.","NitrogenCycleOutput struct separates nitrate_produced_mg_n from tan_oxidized_mg with documentation explicitly noting the distinction and pointing users to tan_oxidized_mg for alkalinity basis.","Alkalinity synchronization test (default_process_preset_alkalinity_matches_core_constant) in tank_data passes, confirming preset and runtime defaults are pinned to NITRIFICATION_ALK_MEQ_PER_MG_N.","Working tree is clean for all committed project files; only .claude/worktrees/tanksim-6e5.4.7 (infrastructure) and uncommitted e2e_shrimp_scenario_probes.rs changes remain, and the latter compiles and passes all 6 tests."],"findings_or_gaps":["Uncommitted working-copy changes exist in e2e_shrimp_scenario_probes.rs (115 insertions, 76 deletions). These compile and pass all 6 tests, but they are not part of the committed deliverable. This was flagged in prior review cycles and persists — low risk since the changes are additive test improvements, not regressions.","Three warm-side temperature curve-shape constants (LOW_TEMP_REPRO_MIN_FACTOR=0.1, HIGH_TEMP_REPRO_SHOULDER_FACTOR=0.5, MIN_REPRO_SUPPRESSION_FACTOR=0.05) remain as file-level named constants rather than species parameters. These are documented as intentionally fixed for the first-pass model (comment at shrimp.rs:1565-1567). The key curve-width parameter (low_temp_repro_ramp_width_c) has been extracted. Acceptable for this deliverable."],"follow_up_or_amendments":["Consider committing or reverting the uncommitted e2e_shrimp_scenario_probes.rs changes to maintain a clean working tree. The changes appear to be improvements from the tanksim-6e5.6.6 work scope and should be tracked there.","If future tuning demands require it, promote the three warm-side temperature curve-shape constants to ShrimpRuntimeParams. Low priority since they are well-documented named constants and the primary curve parameters are already tunable."]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"e184a004-3804-4166-bfd7-4b50bd54a6f6"}
